@ApiHostAddr = http://localhost:5089

### Manual test door. NOT the production path -- sensors go through the edge gateway
### and arrive over gRPC on port 5091. See Features/Ingestion/IngestTelemetryEndpoint.cs.
###
### Omit MessageId and the server generates one, which means re-sending this request
### creates a SECOND reading. Supply your own and re-sending is a no-op, because the
### worker dedupes on it.
POST {{ApiHostAddr}}/api/debug/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "equipmentId": "MANUAL-1",
  "occurredAt": "2026-08-21T12:00:00Z",
  "engineTemperature": 245.0,
  "oilPressure": 42.5
}

### Send this one twice. Both return 202; only one row lands in Postgres.
### That is idempotency, demonstrated in two clicks.
